<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:gpxx="http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/GpxExtensions/v3" xmlns:gpxtpx="http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/TrackPointExtension/v1" creator="Visit Zuid-Limburg" version="1.1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/GpxExtensions/v3 http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/GpxExtensionsv3.xsd http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/TrackPointExtension/v1 http://www.garmin.com/xmlschemas/TrackPointExtensionv1.xsd"><metadata><link href="https://www.visitzuidlimburg.com/experience-zuid-limburg/route/wandelroute-rondom-de-amerikaanse-begraafplaats-margraten/59972/"><text>Wandelroute Rondom de Amerikaanse Begraafplaats Margraten</text></link></metadata><trk><name>Wandelroute Rondom de Amerikaanse Begraafplaats Margraten</name><desc>The landscape around the typical South Limburg town of Margraten is green, rustic and impressive. This walking route through Honthem and Groot-Welsden can be followed via the green posts and shows you the views and locations that you should not miss. Stop for a moment at the American Cemetery, the serene final resting place of the fallen American soldiers who came to the rescue of the Netherlands during the Second World War. You can park in Margraten, where you can also eat freshly baked Limburg flan from the talented kitchen talents of restaurant Talentino.</desc><trkseg><trkpt lat="50.82008" lon="5.82154"><ele>172</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.82002" lon="5.82147"><ele>172</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.8199" lon="5.82118"><ele>171</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.81885" lon="5.82167"><ele>169</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.8187" lon="5.82172"><ele>168</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.81866" lon="5.8217"><ele>167</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.81863" lon="5.82169"><ele>167</ele></trkpt><trkpt lat="50.81861" lon="5.82169"><ele>167</ele></trkpt><trkpt la